From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:45:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: export CoCancelCall, and give it an answer instead of
 a stub.

ole32 exported CoEnableCallCancellation and CoDisableCallCancellation and not
CoCancelCall, the third of the set. combase had it as a stub, so nothing
exported it under the name a caller imports it by.

A delay-load import that cannot be bound does not fail quietly: the helper
raises VcppException(ERROR_SEVERITY_ERROR, ERROR_PROC_NOT_FOUND), 0xc06d007f.
Nobody catches that, so the process dies where it stands.

Measured: Office's Click-to-Run setup.exe delay-imports CoCancelCall from
ole32. Relay-tracing GetProcAddress across an install shows the last call on
the thread that then raised the exception:

  0278:Call KERNEL32.GetProcAddress(79ff0000, "CoCancelCall") ret=00809943
  0278:Ret  KERNEL32.GetProcAddress() retval=00000000
  wine: Unhandled exception 0xc06d007f in thread 278 ... starting debugger...

and setup exits 84 five minutes in, having said nothing about why.

The implementation answers RPC_E_CALL_COMPLETE. Nothing here tracks an
outstanding call, so from this side there is never one left to cancel, and "it
already finished" is the true answer rather than a polite one -- it is what
Windows returns once the call being cancelled has come back, and callers handle
it. The FIXME says what a real cancellation would need.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e441f776f83e4b7e2ec67a3b87fadd0eb28c0b41)

diff --git a/dlls/combase/combase.c b/dlls/combase/combase.c
index 94e256f7cc1..5dda9e5c798 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/combase.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/combase.c
@@ -3450,6 +3450,28 @@ HRESULT WINAPI CoRegisterChannelHook(REFGUID guidExtension, IChannelHook *channe
     return rpc_register_channel_hook(guidExtension, channel_hook);
 }
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           CoCancelCall    (combase.@)
+ *
+ * There is nothing here that tracks an outstanding call, so from this side
+ * there is never one left to cancel and RPC_E_CALL_COMPLETE -- "it already
+ * finished" -- is the true answer rather than a polite one.  Callers handle it:
+ * it is what Windows returns once the call being cancelled has come back.
+ *
+ * What this is really for is existing at all.  Office's Click-to-Run installer
+ * delay-imports CoCancelCall from ole32, which did not export it -- only
+ * combase did, and only as a stub -- so the delay-load helper raised
+ * VcppException(ERROR_PROC_NOT_FOUND), 0xc06d007f, nobody caught it and setup
+ * died on the spot with no message of its own.
+ */
+HRESULT WINAPI CoCancelCall(DWORD thread_id, ULONG timeout)
+{
+    FIXME("%#lx, %lu: no outstanding calls are tracked, reporting the call complete\n",
+          thread_id, timeout);
+
+    return RPC_E_CALL_COMPLETE;
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           CoDisableCallCancellation    (combase.@)
  */
diff --git a/dlls/combase/combase.spec b/dlls/combase/combase.spec
index 19249e17f87..59e5db2aca8 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/combase.spec
+++ b/dlls/combase/combase.spec
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@
 @ stub ClearCleanupFlag
 @ stdcall CoAddRefServerProcess()
 @ stub CoAllowUnmarshalerCLSID
-@ stub CoCancelCall
+@ stdcall CoCancelCall(long long)
 @ stdcall CoCopyProxy(ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall CoCreateErrorInfo(ptr) CreateErrorInfo
 @ stdcall CoCreateFreeThreadedMarshaler(ptr ptr)
diff --git a/dlls/ole32/ole32.spec b/dlls/ole32/ole32.spec
index 6e0c07198c0..29041e869e1 100644
--- a/dlls/ole32/ole32.spec
+++ b/dlls/ole32/ole32.spec
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 @ stdcall CoCreateInstanceEx(ptr ptr long ptr long ptr) combase.CoCreateInstanceEx
 @ stdcall CoCreateInstanceFromApp(ptr ptr long ptr long ptr) combase.CoCreateInstanceFromApp
 @ stdcall CoDecrementMTAUsage(ptr) combase.CoDecrementMTAUsage
+@ stdcall CoCancelCall(long long) combase.CoCancelCall
 @ stdcall CoDisableCallCancellation(ptr) combase.CoDisableCallCancellation
 @ stdcall CoDisconnectObject(ptr long) combase.CoDisconnectObject
 @ stdcall CoDosDateTimeToFileTime(long long ptr) kernel32.DosDateTimeToFileTime
